SUMMARY:FYI: What’s happenin’
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**For Oct 29 thru Nov 4**\nUpcoming **music
  events** may be found here:\nhttps://www.facebook.com/hendolivemusic/\n(U
 pdates on Thurs morning)\n**Assorted entertainment\, festival & market eve
 nts may be found here:**\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/calendar-of-ev
 ents\n**Library programs** may be found here:\nhttps://hendersonpl.libcal.
 com/\n**Wednesday\, October 28**\nWeekly Westie Wednesdays (Ages 21 & Up) 
 (Each Wednesday)\n7-10pm\, Honeysuckle Holler\, 101 East Allen St\, Suite 
 101\, Hendersonville NC 28792\n7-8pm - Continuation Lesson & 7:30-8pm - Be
 ginner Lesson. 8-10pm - Social Dance.\nLessons rotate weekly with our incr
 edible instructor lineup: Ryan Pflumm\, Jason Barnes\, Jenna Shimek\,\nMis
 sy Lindsey\, Rachel Harris\, Tom and Janet Leazenby\, and Tola Sun - all b
 ringing fresh energy and\nperspectives each week! Enjoy a rotation of comm
 unity DJs keeping the vibes high and the floor full all night\nlong. No ou
 tside drinks (including water bottles) - water station available. Outside 
 food welcome. Dress is\ncasual and No partner needed! Dedicated parking ne
 xt to the venue & street parking. Please help us\nsupport our amazing host
  venue by grabbing a drink or snack at the bar - it helps keep dance night
 s thriving!\nPricing: $10 lesson & social\, $5 social only\n**Thu\; Octobe
 r 29\; 6 PM**\nEllen\, Howie & Woody\nSouthern Appalachian Brewery\; 822 L
 ocust St. Hendersonville\n**Friday\, October 30**\nSOUTHERN APPALACHIAN BR
 EWERY \\* The Big Hungry – Night of the Dead (Grateful Dead\, that is...
 ) \\* 7:00 – 9:00\n**Friday\, October 30**\nBlake Ellege\n8-11pm\, Oklaw
 aha Brewery\, 147 First Ave East\, Hendersonville\n**October 31 @ 3:00 pm 
 - 4:30 pm**\nReader’s Theatre – **War of the Worlds\, The 1938 Radio S
 cript**\n**Tickets:** https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/readers-theatr
 e-war-of-the-worlds\nBroadcast from New York’s Mercury Theatre in 1938\,
  this infamous radio play\, based on the novel by H. G. Wells\, had many t
 errified listeners convinced that an actual alien invasion of Earth was ta
 king place. Adapted by Howard E. Koch\, co-writer of Casablanca\, and dire
 cted and narrated by Orson Welles\, this original script detailing the fri
 ghtening tale of an extraterrestrial takeover is now available to bring to
  life onstage to thrill and chill audiences.\nhttps://visithendersonvillen
 c.org/event/readers-theatre-war-of-the-worlds-the-1938-radio-script/2026-1
 0-31\nhttps://hendersonvilletheatre.org/readers-theatre-war-of-the-worlds-
 the-1938-radio-script/\n**Saturday\, October 31**\nTreat Street\; 2:00 pm 
 - 5:00 pm\; Free\nJoin for Kids Fun Zone – Sponsored by Biltmore Church\
 , Trick-Or-Treating\, DJ Dance Party\, Costume contest\, Games and more.\n
 **Saturday\, October 31**\nSaints & Sinners - Halloween Costume Party\n6-1
 0pm\, Sissy’s/J&M Farms\, 3016 Chimney Rock Road\, Hendersonville\n**Sat
 urday\, October 31**\nFlashback Band Halloween Extravaganza\n6:30-9:30pm\,
  Mills River Brewery\, 336 Banner Farm Rd\, Mills River\n**October 31** @ 
 6:00 pm - 9:00 pm\; Free\nHalloween Party at Trailside Brewing Co.\na spoo
 ktacular night of music\, costumes\, and Halloween fun at Trailside Brewin
 g with Steve Weams and The Ghouls!\nLive Music: Steve Weams Band and the G
 houls\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/halloween-party-at-trailsid
 e-brewing-co\n**Wednesday\, Nov 4**\nJason DeCristofaro's Jazz Night (Each
  Wednesday)\n6-8pm\, Southern Appalachian Brewery\, 822 Locust St\, Hender
 sonville\n**November 6 - November 18**\nOur Town – An Art Exhibition\nat
  Art MoB Studios\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/our-town-an-art-
 exhibition-celebrating-henderson-county\nhttps://www.artmobstudios.com/\n*
 *November 7** @ 9:00 am - 2:00 pm\; Free\n**Holiday Craft Fair & Bake Sale
  in Etowah NC**\nhosted by Etowah United Methodist Church. Now celebrating
  its 42nd year\, this beloved community tradition offers a festive day of 
 handmade gifts\, baked goods\, and holiday cheer — all while supporting 
 local missions.\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/holiday-craft-fai
 r\n\nThese are NOT hosted events and are posted for informational purposes
  only. Please make personal arrangements to meetup with friends and family
 .\nIf you wish to attend and host one of these events\, I will post the ev
 ent as an individual happening. Hosting only requires being focal point fo
 r others and making introductions. Simple!!
