SUMMARY:Blue Ridge Symphonic Brass Fall Concert
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nGreetings\, friends and music lovers... We 
 are pleased to announce dates for our upcoming concert season\, and hope t
 hat you will join us!\n\nThe first concert will take place on Sunday\, Nov
 ember 1 at Brevard First United Methodist Church\, [325 N. Broad St](https
 ://www.google.com/maps/search/325+N.+Broad+St?entry=gmail&source=g).\, and
  will begin at 3:00 PM. You are also invited to attend a reception followi
 ng the concert\, so please plan now to attend.\n\nMaestro Hairston has pla
 nned a wonderfully varied program that will include selections such as *Ha
 llelujah Fanfare* that features three antiphonal groups of brass\; *Promen
 ade* from Mussorgsky's "Pictures at an Exhibition"\; the toe-tapping *Big 
 Brass Blues\;* an original version of the hymn *O For a Thousand Tongues t
 o Sing* followed by a stirring 1995 arrangement of the tune by composer Jo
 an Pinkston - and more!\n\nWe do hope to see you there\, and if you could 
 invite your friends\, family\, neighbors and co-workers we would be most a
 ppreciative.
