SUMMARY:Butter Gap Loop\; a Saunter
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nWe will begin behind the fish hatchery up t
 he Cedar Rock Tr\, visit only 1 Cedar Rock Falls side trails\, visit the a
 bandoned beaver dam pond\, connect with the Butter Gap and return downhill
  on the (newly developed mountain bike friendly) Buttergap switchbacks. He
 avily forested ‘natural' surface with occasional rock & roots.\nUp to 12
  ppl are welcome to join us. Remember - hikes led by ‘the Curmudgeon’ 
 tend to have pleasant surprises.\nDifficulty: All the climb is in the 1st 
 half of the loop. Bridges cross the streams. The downhill from the high po
 int is constant. **Popular mountain biker section.**\n**Geriatrics are ask
 ed to bring their own BP cuffs.**\nWe are the **Sloth Hike Team of WNC**: 
 “We will get there when we get there.” We dare to go where the ‘real
 ’ hike groups don’t ***!!***\n***https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bf5Tg
 VRGND4***\nHike Details:\n**Social ‘hour’ at 10 AM. Cattle Call at 10:
 10 AM**\nHike Distance: 3.2 miles\; Accum ascent: 600 ft\; Pace: **1.5mph*
 *\n**Return Not earlier than: 12:30PM (=2.75 hrs)**\n**THIS IS A DOG-PARTI
 CIPANT HIKE.** This event is ***NOT*** for those who are uncomfortable wit
 h the antics of fun-loving dogs. Well trained dogs **(you don’t have to 
 yell)** can be 'off-leash'. 'On leash' in vicinity of other hike groups.\n
 Incessant prattlers will be assumed to be having an affair.\nWeather Check
 : Brevard\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nI currentl
 y have 1 driver(s) (=???ppl)\n..All hikes are at your own risk. You are re
 sponsible for your OWN safety and adequate equipment.\nWaiver: : The organ
 izer of this event is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The functi
 on of the organizer is only to organize this event. There are certain risk
 s inherent in any outdoor activity. Each participant\, by signing up to at
 tend this event\, agrees to release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo F
 un Friends\, its Partners\, Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, in
 jury\, illness\, or personal loss which might occur while participating in
  this activity or while traveling in any vehicle during this trip. **Each 
 participant further agrees to abide by the rules and regulations concernin
 g safety\, to follow instructions of the leader(s)\, and not to become int
 entionally separated from the group.** The leader(s) also has the right to
  use any images collected on this trip for recording on website photo coll
 ections.\ngordie's contact: CurmudgeonHiker@gmail.com\n(**before** day of 
 hike): 828.393.0297 (text only)\n**Pics: https://www.flickr.com/photos/146
 993931@N05/albums**
